# Accessibility and Pagefind

When editing Astro layouts, pages, or components:

1. Keep `lang="en-GB"` on the document root in `BaseLayout`.
2. Mark indexable main content with `data-pagefind-body`.
3. Keep chrome and non-content UI out of search with `data-pagefind-ignore`
   (header, footer, search widget, and `pagefindIgnore` pages such as 404).
4. Preserve `aria-current="page"` on active nav links.
5. For external links, use `target="_blank"` with
   `rel="noopener noreferrer"`, visible text, and
   `<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>`.
6. Keep focus styling tied to `--color-focus` / existing focus rules.
7. Do not strip these attributes or classes when refactoring markup.
